# Fixed-width initializer rejects an out-of-range cast element

Verifies a cast feeding a fixed-width initializer keeps the existing `->to`
conversion semantics: converting `300` to `int8` fails because the requested
representation cannot hold the magnitude, so the element cannot enter the
`int8[]` array.

>>> source
let source: int64 = 300
let a: int8[] = [source->to(int8)]
print(a[0])

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: runtime error: cannot convert `int64` to `int8`

<<< exit
1
